youranmod.jei.locator_module.info=Locator module (a location peripheral): goes into the locator slot of a computer. When a website asks for this computer's location, a system confirmation box appears first (outside the computer screen, web pages cannot click it); if you agree, the server signs a location proof with the computer's dimension and coordinates and hands it to the website, which checks it against the public key (location.yr). Without it the computer still gets online; only websites that need the location will not work. Temporary recipe; it will change when computer manufacturing is added.
